# The camera: zoom in on a curve until it looks straight (the idea behind the derivative).
title "Zoom in until it's straight"
schema axes x=[-1,4] y=[-1,9] xlabel="x" ylabel="y"
mark f path fn={x^2} label="y = x²"
mark p dot x=1 y=1 label="(1, 1)"
Say: "Here is a curve, and one |pt|point on it."
@pt indicate p
Say: "Let's zoom |in|in, closer and closer."
@in camera zoom=6 on=f x=1
Say: "Closer |more|still."
@more camera zoom=60 on=f x=1
Say: "Up close, the curve is a straight line with |slope|slope two."
@slope mark t line x1=0.95 y1=0.9 x2=1.05 y2=1.1 label="slope 2"
Say: "Now step |back|back."
@back camera reset
